-- title:
--   Removing a null cell from a partition
-- statement:
--   Let $\gamma_d$ be the standard Gaussian measure on $\mathbb R^d$. A partition into $k$ cells is a family of measurable sets $A_1,\dots,A_k$ such that almost every point lies in exactly one of them. Its value is $\sum_i|z(A_i)|^2$, where $z(A)=\int_Ax\,d\gamma_d$. If $A_0,\dots,A_k$ is a partition and $\gamma_d(A_i)=0$, then the family obtained by deleting $A_i$,
--   $$
--   \bigl(A_j\bigr)_{j\ne i},
--   $$
--   is a partition into $k$ cells.
--
--   Since a null cell has centroid $0$, the value is unchanged, which allows induction on the number of cells.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/GaussianPropeller/Elimination.lean#L92-L107

